<title>POLAND: Most Polish min t-bill prices flat, 8-wk bill up.</title>
<headline>Most Polish min t-bill prices flat, 8-wk bill up.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Minimum prices of most Polish T-bills held flat at today's primary auction on total demand of 1.17 billion zlotys against a one billion zloty offer, the finance ministry said.</p>
<p>The treasury sold 740 million zlotys worth of bills.</p>
<p>   T-bill	    8-week  13-week  26-week  39-week  52-week</p>
<p>   new min price   97.26    95.50    91.18     ---     83.57</p>
<p>   (pvs auction) *(92.21)  (95.50)  (91.18)    ---    (83.57)</p>
<p>   new max price   97.30    95.58    91.27     ---     83.65</p>
<p>   (pvs auction)  (97.30)  (95.65)  (91.30)    ---    (83.72)</p>
<p>   offer	     150.0    200.0    150.0     ---     550.0</p>
<p>   bids recorded   289.9    151.1    102.9     ---     627.8</p>
<p>   bids accepted   159.4    106.1     61.9     ---     413.1</p>
<p>   next auction    250.0    200.0    150.0     ---     600.0</p>
<p>NOTE: Offer, bids in million zlotys.</p>
<p>* Last offered on September 23.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
